{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Experiment result (2026-09-07, scratch worktree at origin/main 4c77d6f3e96f, `git mv src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler src/rebar/reconciler` only, no import edits):\n- C901 scores are path-independent: after the move `--check` reports the six functions as `new` at the new path with scores 32, 20, 27, 27, 16, 23, identical to their scores at the old path on the clean tree; the old keys bucket `stale`. (`apply` at 20 and `create_one` at 27 are already under their ceilings 22 and 36 on main, so they were already stale there.)\n- The re-spell must RE-SORT the ceilings map, not just substitute the prefix: a plain in-place `sed` fails `--check` with `error: 'ceilings' keys must be sorted`, because `src/rebar/reconciler/...` sorts after `src/rebar/_engine_support/...`, `_ids.py`, `_mcp_reads.py` and the other underscore-prefixed keys. Rewrite the file through `render_baseline` (or `json.dumps(..., indent=2, sort_keys=True)` matching its format); `git diff --stat` then shows 6 insertions, 6 deletions.\n- After the sorted re-spell: `--check` gives `active=33 new=0 increased=0 stale=16`, byte-for-byte the clean tree's summary (the 16 stale rows pre-exist on main and are not this story's to drain), and `pytest tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py -q` passes (87 passed).\n- The lock against main's copy (`--lock --base <main's baseline>`) prints exactly six `complexity-baseline lock: NEW entry added: 'src/rebar/reconciler/...'` lines plus the administrator hint and exits 1; removed old-path entries are not flagged. This confirms the landing instruction above: the lock step is the one expected red item for the operator's force-submit.\n- `rebar._proc.reap_process_group(proc, *, grace, drain, label, logger)` exists at `src/rebar/_proc.py:38`; two thin `_reap_process_group` wrappers in `adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py:507` and `jira_family/wiki_render.py:417` import it lazily and move with the package."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788813374091445754,"uuid":"6accbb1a-d8c7-4fc0-ac61-d44190e8d82d"}